# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repo's blobs are LF, but a Windows checkout materialises them as CRLF
# (core.autocrlf=true), which makes `npm run format:check` report every file as
# unformatted and `prettier --write` churn the whole tree. These rules pin the
# working copy to LF so local formatting matches what CI (Linux) sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending-converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
